    "task_title": "Book a table for 20 people tomorrow evening for Can; if they need a person to confirm, connect Can",
    "task_goal": "RESTAURANT TRIAL TASK GUIDANCE (MIT-018 route A) \u2014 load into the approved call task before dialing.\nThese are instructions for this one attended trial, not facts about any restaurant.\n\nMode: owner. Task: Can would like a table for 20 people tomorrow evening. If they\nneed a person to confirm, connect Can. The restaurant's phone may first be\nanswered by an automated AI assistant; the engine answers it only with its fixed\nstaff request. Wait for a staff member, then ring and bridge the approved owner.\nDo not confirm, change or cancel a reservation yourself, pay, give card or deposit\ndetails, or accept terms. Never invent a name, phone number, time, date or any\ndetail. Disclose that you are an AI assistant.\n\nCallback is NOT authorized. Do not accept a callback, a text message or a link, and\ndo not give any phone number. While on hold or during a transfer, stay silent.\nRing only the separately approved owner destination. Wait for private owner\nacceptance before bridging. If the owner declines or does not answer, or the\nrestaurant hangs up, follow the approved one-question fallback and then end; no\nautomatic retry. Respect the trial's global 10-minute deadline and balance stop.\n\nApproved decision A overrides the older no-fallback instruction: after the owner timeout, ask only the engine-enforced fallback question, then end. Restrictions: no callback, no payment, no booking, change or cancellation; never invent identity or booking.\nApproval restrictions: confirm, change or cancel a reservation, payment, deposit or card details, invent identity or details, accept callback",
